# Story 59.14 — English and Arabic: setup screens, messages, and the install guides on maktaba.tv

> Epic 59 · Phase 4 (strings land with each story) · Depends on: 59.01–59.13

## Why

Every user-facing string ships in English and Arabic, in the web and in the native apps. This
epic adds many such strings:
- setup steps;
- permission states and fixes in each NAS's own words;
- hardware tiers;
- isolation levels;
- update messages.

It also adds install guides that a NAS owner will follow step by step. maktaba.tv is where
households install and learn Maktaba. maktaba.dev is the developer wiki.

# Story 59.15 — CI on NAS-shaped containers, device checklists, logs kept

> Epic 59 · Phase 1 (grows each phase) · Depends on: 59.01 · Needed by: every story's tests

## Why

Most NAS failures come from a handful of differences, and each one can be imitated in a
container on a GitHub runner:
- another uid;
- a read-only or foreign-owned share;
- a memory limit;
- arm64;
- a kernel without Landlock;
- a render device or none.

What cannot be imitated needs a short written checklist on a real device: DSM's ACL dialogs,
TrueNAS's app install, real Quick Sync, a real DSM kernel.

